From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:03:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/25] Coherent: tell trapping surfaces of host reads and
 writes, test B1, add guest probes

- P1: the video devices read and write guest surfaces outside the runtime
  (lends, and the dma-buf a decoder or the scaler binds in place), which
  bypassed the traps: a host read missed GPU writes still in the image, a
  host write never reached it. lend_surface_bytes{,_for_reading} and the new
  GuestSurface::device_reads/device_writes (decoder frame writes, scaler
  source and destination in place) now call shadow_coherent::host_reads /
  host_writes over the surface's view and each run of its pages.
- B1: vendor/qemu census tracks the rows as ranges (93f37d5d3a);
  coherent_test.c tracks only the rows, and t_outside_write, t_outside_dma
  and the new t_planes run in the full harness (CENSUS_OUTSIDE=1/2/3 alone).
- Guest probes for the Mac (untested, no swiftc here): probe_encode (P1),
  probe_untracked (P2), probe_signal, probe_tail (B1), probe_long.
- Cargo [patch] points at the coherent-b1 m2v worktree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
